# gcloud builds submit (Node images from REPO_ROOT) honors .gcloudignore
# (else .gitignore), not .dockerignore. Keep this in lockstep with
# .dockerignore so the Cloud Build upload matches the context CI and local
# `docker build -f … .` exercise.
#
# IDENTICAL TEXT IS NOT IDENTICAL MEANING — every root-only entry below MUST
# carry a leading slash. This file is gitignore syntax, where a bare `docs`
# matches a directory named docs at ANY depth; .dockerignore anchors bare
# patterns to the context root. A bare `docs` here therefore silently stripped
# web/app/docs/** and web/components/docs/** from the Cloud Build upload while
# every local and CI `docker build` kept them. Next then built cleanly — pages
# and the components they import vanished together, so nothing dangled — and
# shipped 11 routes instead of 21. The header's /docs link went live against a
# route that had never been compiled, and /docs 404'd in production from #101
# until this was found. Docker Cleans leading slashes away, so `/docs` means
# root-only in BOTH files: anchor here, mirror there, and the two stay honest.
#
# This file is ONLY consulted when the upload top-level is the repo root
# (gcp.sh build_node_image). API deploys use `cd api && --source .`, so
# they resolve api/.gcloudignore and are unaffected by the `api` exclude
# below — see test_api_deploy_source_is_api_dir_not_repo_root.
.git
.github
.worktrees
.claude
.superpowers
**/node_modules
**/.next
**/.next-auth-entry-test
**/__pycache__
**/.venv
**/venv
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/*.pyc
/api
/docs
/data
/out
/reports
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
HANDOFF.md
README.md
LICENSE.md
Makefile
**/*.md
!web/package.json
!console/package.json
